ERRATUM for arm-C-legacy-7feb4af2.json (#1619, 2026-09-16)

`queryCostMs.p50` and `queryCostMs.p95` in that file are BOTH THE MAXIMUM, not
percentiles. The capture predates commit a34eec38, which fixed the call into
`percentile` (it takes a FRACTION; the arm axis passed 50 and 95, so
`Math.ceil(309 * 50) - 1` clamped to the last index of the sorted samples).

  as recorded   p50 = p95 = 424.21 ms   -- the slowest of the 309 queries
  true values   p50 = 43.41 ms, p95 = 58.40 ms

The true values are re-derived from the 309 per-query `ms` values inside the
file itself (nearest rank, `eval/latency-stats.ts`). The measured rows are left
exactly as captured, so the file still parses through `parseArmRunReport` and
every other figure it carries -- recallAtK, mrr, imageNegativeLeakAt1 -- is
correct and re-derives exactly under the shipped definitions.

This file is the legacy-revision C control (ADR-027 amendment A-3), captured at
7feb4af2. It is identical to arm-C-7e01cf2e.json on every METRIC, query for
query; the rows are not byte-equal, and the README in this directory says why.

`pinParticipatingQueries: 0` beside `rag_pin_identifiers: true` is
configuration on, zero in effect: no query in the DE image fixture is an exact
identifier, so #1107's pin never fired.

The `command` field records the ABSOLUTE `--out` path this run was actually
given:

  /Users/simon/localGIT/compendiq/compendiq-ce-1619/backend/src/domains/llm/eval/artifacts/1611/arm-C-legacy-7feb4af2.json

The sibling capture records a repo-relative one. This string is left exactly as
captured: `command` is a provenance field, so a tidied one would record a
command line that was never run. Future runs should pass a repo-relative
`--out` from `backend/`.

Full context: README.md in this directory, "Errata on these two files".
